 "summary": "Statements sit at the natural level: hypotheses are minimal (`F1_nonneg` and `sqrt_mul_abs_F3_le_two_mul_F1` carry none; `hQ2`/`hx` appear only where `Real.sq_sqrt` or the `2x` factor needs them), general results are proved first and specialized (`two_mul_mul_sq_apply_long_le` in the free row index, `crossSectionBracket_nonneg` feeding the two cross-section corollaries, `abs_mul_Yminus_mul_sqrt_le` in an abstract `G \u2265 0` and `|s| \u2264 1`), and `Matrix.PosSemidef.sq_apply_le` is derived from Tau Ceti's RCLike `normSq_le` while `two_mul_abs_apply_le` drops its now-unneeded `[Finite n]`. No unused or too-strong assumption, and no special-case proof duplicated for something the PR also proves in general.",
